  "prefLabel": "Agr 201.01 Purpose",
  "priorExpiration": "2004-07-25",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Agr 201.01 Purpose. The commissioner of agriculture, markets & food or designated agent conducts various proceedings for the purpose of acquiring sufficient information to make fair and reasoned decisions on matters within the commissioner's statutory jurisdiction, including decisions on applications for licensure and complaints filed against licensees. These rules are construed to secure the just, efficient and accurate resolution of all department proceedings.\n\nSource. #2298, eff 2-17-83; ss by #2855, eff 9-24-84, EXPIRED 9-24-90\n\nNew. #6299, eff 7-25-96, EXPIRED: 7-25-04\n\nNew. #8309-A, eff 3-24-05",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/agr200.html"
